      "status": "COMPLETED",
      "content": "Done. `workspace/mass_report.json` is written:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"main_part_mass\": 34648.041235,\n  \"material_id\": 42\n}\n```\n\n**How it was derived:**\n1. **Parsing** — 352 triangles from the binary STL; the 2-byte attribute field holds the Material ID.\n2. **Debris filtering** — 53 connected components found. The largest (128 triangles, a closed watertight solid, bbox 20×20×20) is the main part; the other 52 are 4-triangle debris fragments (material IDs 0/1).\n3. **Material** — all 128 main-part triangles carry Material ID **42** → Unobtanium, density **5.55 g/cm³**.\n4. **Mass** — volume 6242.890312594918 cm³ × 5.55 g/cm³ = **34648.041235 g**.\n\nI also independently re-parsed the file (exact and quantized vertex matching) and it reproduced the identical component count, largest component, and volume to 6 decimal places, so the result is comfortably within the 0.1% tolerance.",
      "text": "Done. `workspace/mass_report.json` is written:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"main_part_mass\": 34648.041235,\n  \"material_id\": 42\n}\n```\n\n**How it was derived:**\n1. **Parsing** — 352 triangles from the binary STL; the 2-byte attribute field holds the Material ID.\n2. **Debris filtering** — 53 connected components found. The largest (128 triangles, a closed watertight solid, bbox 20×20×20) is the main part; the other 52 are 4-triangle debris fragments (material IDs 0/1).\n3. **Material** — all 128 main-part triangles carry Material ID **42** → Unobtanium, density **5.55 g/cm³**.\n4. **Mass** — volume 6242.890312594918 cm³ × 5.55 g/cm³ = **34648.041235 g**.\n\nI also independently re-parsed the file (exact and quantized vertex matching) and it reproduced the identical component count, largest component, and volume to 6 decimal places, so the result is comfortably within the 0.1% tolerance.",
